### Type Predicate Inference for Truthiness Checks (TypeScript)

Source: https://github.com/context7/typescriptlang/blob/main/handbook/release-notes/typescript-5-5.md

Demonstrates how TypeScript 5.5 infers type predicates for object types based on truthiness checks. Functions must return a boolean. Previously, a filter operation on a number array might have resulted in a broader type; now, it can infer a more precise type, potentially breaking existing code if not explicitly handled with type annotations.

```tsx
// Previously, nums: (number | null)[]
// Now, nums: number[]
const nums = [1, 2, 3, null, 5].filter(x => x !== null);
nums.push(null);  // ok in TS 5.4, error in TS 5.5
```

```tsx
const nums: (number | null)[] = [1, 2, 3, null, 5].filter(x => x !== null);
nums.push(null);  // ok in all versions
```

